  "title": "Journal v2: schema-validated, indexed, replayable event log",
  "summary": "The journal grows from a two-payload buffer into a versioned, schema-validated event log. Events now carry a typed actor, an optional work item and change, and an optional cost; eight payload types replace the original two. Every append is validated against a draft 2020-12 JSON schema before a byte is written, and a run-complete event must name the journal's current head hash. The buffer directory becomes runs/, and the first accepted event of a work-item-scoped run records that run in a per-work-item index. A new reader replays a run's chain, refusing any line that is malformed, schema-invalid, at an unknown version, or off the chain.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
